1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,700
What if it
rained nonstop,

2
00:00:02,090 --> 00:00:04,710
everywhere on
Earth, for a year?

3
00:00:04,710 --> 00:00:07,050
Today, rain
is patchy:

4
00:00:07,050 --> 00:00:08,330
storms come and go,

5
00:00:08,330 --> 00:00:11,340
and most of the Sahara
stays bone dry.

6
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:16,160
The sky holds surprisingly
little water.

7
00:00:16,160 --> 00:00:18,360
All of it would
cover Earth just two

8
00:00:18,360 --> 00:00:20,570
and a half
centimeters deep.

9
00:00:21,050 --> 00:00:23,730
So rain must
be recycled.

10
00:00:23,730 --> 00:00:26,130
Sunlight lifts
water from the sea,

11
00:00:26,130 --> 00:00:29,050
about a meter's
worth every year.

12
00:00:29,050 --> 00:00:30,150
Spread evenly,

13
00:00:30,150 --> 00:00:31,830
that's a gentle
drizzle:

14
00:00:31,830 --> 00:00:34,340
about three
millimeters a day.

15
00:00:34,610 --> 00:00:36,630
Much of the Sahara
would get dozens

16
00:00:36,630 --> 00:00:39,330
of times its
usual rain.

17
00:00:39,330 --> 00:00:41,590
It could turn
green again,

18
00:00:41,590 --> 00:00:44,160
as it was eight
thousand years ago.

19
00:00:44,630 --> 00:00:46,370
Yet rainforests,

20
00:00:46,370 --> 00:00:48,790
used to two meters
or more a year,

21
00:00:48,790 --> 00:00:50,740
would actually
get less.

22
00:00:51,110 --> 00:00:54,330
Farmers would lose
their dry days.

23
00:00:54,330 --> 00:00:56,530
Grain can rot
before harvest,

24
00:00:56,530 --> 00:00:58,190
and solar panels
would dim

25
00:00:58,190 --> 00:01:00,940
under a sky that
never clears.

26
00:01:01,310 --> 00:01:02,930
Here's the twist:

27
00:01:02,930 --> 00:01:05,030
those clouds would
block the sunlight

28
00:01:05,030 --> 00:01:07,330
that drives
evaporation,

29
00:01:07,330 --> 00:01:10,520
so the rain itself
would slowly weaken.

30
00:01:10,990 --> 00:01:13,800
Even endless rain
needs the Sun.
